  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The given statement is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8743;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>~</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8744;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>~</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Let us take&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mi>c</mi></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8746;</mo><mfenced><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msup></mfenced></math>.</p><p>Now let us apply distributive law to the above statement.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8801;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8746;</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8745;</mo><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo>&#8746;</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msup></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8801;</mo><mfenced><mi>U</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8745;</mo><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo>&#8746;</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msup></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8801;</mo><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo>&#8746;</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msup></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Now the given statement&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8743;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>~</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8744;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>~</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;will be equivalent to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>~</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>p</mi></math>&nbsp;or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>~</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>q</mi></math>.</p><p>Hence the given statement is equivalent to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>~</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>q</mi></math>,</p><p>Now negation of given statement by demorgan&#39;s law will be,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>~</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>~</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8801;</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8743;</mo><mi>q</mi></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
